1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,779
Ava: A team can train a model with PyTorch and still face a lot of work before serving it.
Ava：团队可以用 PyTorch 训练模型，但要将模型投入服务，仍有大量工作要做。

2
00:00:05,779 --> 00:00:09,858
That's why this membership announcement caught my attention.
所以这则成员资格公告引起了我的注意。

3
00:00:09,858 --> 00:00:17,822
Nebius has joined the PyTorch Foundation as a Platinum member, and its work touches both training and inference.
Nebius 已作为白金成员加入 PyTorch 基金会，其工作涉及训练和推理。

4
00:00:17,822 --> 00:00:24,948
Brian: The useful question is what Nebius already does and what it plans to do through the Foundation.
Brian：关键是看 Nebius 已经在做什么，以及计划通过基金会做什么。

5
00:00:24,948 --> 00:00:32,074
Startups and enterprises use PyTorch to train and fine-tune models at scale on Nebius AI Cloud.
初创企业和大型企业在 Nebius AI Cloud 上使用 PyTorch，大规模训练和微调模型。

6
00:00:32,074 --> 00:00:38,500
Nebius also supports work on vLLM, a Foundation project concerned with inference.
Nebius 也支持基金会旗下的推理项目 vLLM。

7
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,210
Ava: Let's make that concrete.
Ava：说具体一点。

8
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:45,476
Imagine a team fine-tuning a model for a product, then preparing to serve it.
假设一个团队为产品微调模型，接着准备将其投入服务。

9
00:00:45,476 --> 00:00:48,554
They'd have questions at more than one stage.
他们在多个阶段都会遇到问题。

10
00:00:48,554 --> 00:00:57,522
The announcement connects Nebius to that broad workflow, though it doesn't say every customer uses every part of its platform.
公告将 Nebius 与这一完整流程联系起来，但没有说每位客户都会使用其平台的所有部分。

11
00:00:57,522 --> 00:01:04,679
Brian: Nebius describes its AI cloud platform as covering data and model training through production deployment.
Brian：Nebius 称，其 AI 云平台覆盖从数据处理、模型训练到生产部署的流程。

12
00:01:04,679 --> 00:01:06,519
That's the company's scope.
这是该公司所说的平台覆盖范围。

13
00:01:06,519 --> 00:01:12,790
The more specific statement is that customers train and fine-tune with PyTorch on its cloud.
更具体的说法是，客户在其云平台上使用 PyTorch 训练和微调模型。

14
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:18,320
Its inference and post-training contributions are another part of the story.
它在推理和后训练方面的贡献，则是另一部分。

15
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:23,572
Ava: I want to understand why the Foundation is the setting for this announcement.
Ava：我想弄清楚，为什么这项公告是在基金会的背景下发布的。

16
00:01:23,572 --> 00:01:28,824
Nebius runs a cloud, but the software involved reaches well beyond one cloud.
Nebius 运营云平台，但相关软件的应用远不止于一家云服务商。

17
00:01:28,824 --> 00:01:31,757
The Foundation calls itself vendor-neutral.
基金会称自己是供应商中立的组织。

18
00:01:31,757 --> 00:01:35,518
How does that shape the role of a Platinum member?
这会如何影响白金成员的角色？

19
00:01:35,518 --> 00:01:41,741
Brian: The PyTorch Foundation is a community-driven hub hosted by the Linux Foundation.
Brian：PyTorch 基金会由 Linux 基金会托管，是一个由社区驱动的协作平台。

20
00:01:41,741 --> 00:01:50,143
It supports the core PyTorch framework and projects including vLLM, DeepSpeed, Ray, Helion, and Safetensors.
它支持 PyTorch 核心框架，以及 vLLM、DeepSpeed、Ray、Helion 和 Safetensors 等项目。

21
00:01:50,143 --> 00:01:58,116
Its stated scope covers training, optimizing, serving, and running models across chips and clouds.
按其说法，工作范围涵盖跨芯片和云平台的模型训练、优化、服务和运行。

22
00:01:58,116 --> 00:02:05,032
Ava: So membership puts Nebius in a community that works on several parts of our imagined team's path.
Ava：也就是说，加入基金会让 Nebius 进入了一个参与我们设想的团队多个工作阶段的社区。

23
00:02:05,032 --> 00:02:08,953
That doesn't turn a membership into a software feature.
但成为成员本身并不等于增加了一项软件功能。

24
00:02:08,953 --> 00:02:15,506
I find the existing work more useful for understanding what Nebius brings to the table.
我觉得现有工作更能说明 Nebius 能带来什么。

25
00:02:15,506 --> 00:02:17,049
Brian: One example is vLLM.
Brian：vLLM 就是一个例子。

26
00:02:17,049 --> 00:02:23,223
Nebius has long provided compute for its development, testing, and benchmarking.
Nebius 长期为它的开发、测试和基准测试提供算力。

27
00:02:23,223 --> 00:02:29,243
The announcement includes multi-node work on large models such as DeepSeek R1.
公告还提到针对 DeepSeek R1 等大型模型开展的多节点工作。

28
00:02:29,243 --> 00:02:37,696
Providing compute for those activities is a concrete form of support; it isn't itself a benchmark result.
为这些活动提供算力是具体的支持，但这本身不是基准测试结果。

29
00:02:37,696 --> 00:02:39,340
Ava: That distinction matters.
Ava：这个区别很重要。

30
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:44,931
If I hear that a company helped with benchmarking, I might expect a speed comparison.
听说一家公司协助做基准测试，我可能会期待看到速度对比。

31
00:02:44,931 --> 00:02:50,719
But the statement we can use here establishes the support and the kind of work involved.
但这里的表述只说明它提供了支持，以及涉及哪类工作。

32
00:02:50,719 --> 00:02:55,278
It doesn't give our imagined team a number for its own workload.
它没有给我们设想的团队提供适用于自身工作负载的数字。

33
00:02:55,278 --> 00:02:58,137
Brian: There's work beyond supplying compute.
Brian：它做的不只是提供算力。

34
00:02:58,137 --> 00:03:05,887
Nebius's Applied AI team contributes inference and post-training optimizations to open-source projects.
Nebius 的应用 AI 团队还为开源项目贡献推理和后训练优化。

35
00:03:05,887 --> 00:03:13,561
The announcement also says Nebius's open-source work has been incorporated into the PyTorch Ecosystem.
公告还说，Nebius 的开源工作已被纳入 PyTorch 生态系统。

36
00:03:13,561 --> 00:03:20,156
Those are existing activities, distinct from the performance work Nebius now plans.
这些都是现有工作，有别于 Nebius 现在计划开展的性能优化工作。

37
00:03:20,156 --> 00:03:24,006
Ava: For a framework engineer, that distinction is practical.
Ava：对框架工程师来说，这个区别有实际意义。

38
00:03:24,006 --> 00:03:27,581
Compute support can help a project develop and test.
算力支持能帮助项目开发和测试。

39
00:03:27,581 --> 00:03:31,706
An optimization contribution can change software people use.
优化贡献则可能改变人们使用的软件。

40
00:03:31,706 --> 00:03:41,338
Here, we know the contribution areas, so we can discuss the engineering direction without assigning a particular mechanism to the work.
这里我们知道贡献涉及哪些领域，因此可以讨论工程方向，无须推断具体实现机制。

41
00:03:41,338 --> 00:03:43,419
Brian: It gives us a starting point.
Brian：这给了我们一个讨论的起点。

42
00:03:43,419 --> 00:03:53,249
Nebius has experience with PyTorch training workloads, vLLM development support, and open-source work around inference and post-training.
Nebius 有支持 PyTorch 训练任务、vLLM 开发，以及参与推理和后训练开源工作的经验。

43
00:03:53,249 --> 00:03:56,693
Those activities make its plans easier to place.
这些工作让它的计划更容易理解。

44
00:03:56,693 --> 00:04:02,424
They don't mean every stage of a customer's workflow uses the same project.
但这不意味着客户流程的每个阶段都使用同一个项目。

45
00:04:02,424 --> 00:04:06,912
Ava: The new plan is about performance on the latest hardware platforms.
Ava：新计划聚焦于在最新硬件平台上的性能。

46
00:04:06,912 --> 00:04:10,663
I hear two project names in that plan: PyTorch and vLLM.
我听到了两个项目名称：PyTorch 和 vLLM。

47
00:04:10,663 --> 00:04:20,726
That seems relevant to teams working from model training toward serving, but the two projects would give an engineer different things to examine.
这似乎与从模型训练走向服务的团队有关，但工程师对这两个项目的考察重点会不同。

48
00:04:20,726 --> 00:04:26,800
Brian: Yes. Nebius plans to contribute to PyTorch and vLLM performance on those platforms.
Brian：是的。Nebius 计划为提升 PyTorch 和 vLLM 在这些平台上的性能作出贡献。

49
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:34,044
It also plans to share what it learns from running inference and post-training at production scale.
它还计划分享大规模生产环境中运行推理和后训练任务的经验。

50
00:04:34,044 --> 00:04:36,678
That's a statement of intended work.
这些说的是计划开展的工作。

51
00:04:36,678 --> 00:04:42,004
A future contribution would let engineers examine the actual change.
未来若有具体贡献，工程师就能审视实际改动。

52
00:04:42,004 --> 00:04:44,657
Ava: The production experience interests me.
Ava：我对生产环境中的经验很感兴趣。

53
00:04:44,657 --> 00:04:51,800
A team running inference repeatedly can encounter problems that weren't obvious during model development.
反复运行推理的团队，可能遇到模型开发阶段未显现的问题。

54
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:57,650
If Nebius shares what it learns, that could help frame work in an open-source project.
如果 Nebius 分享经验，就能帮助开源项目确定工作重点。

55
00:04:57,650 --> 00:05:02,082
I'm treating that as a possibility, not an announced result.
我说的只是一种可能，并非已公布的成果。

56
00:05:02,082 --> 00:05:03,548
Brian: That's a fair reading.
Brian：这样理解很公允。

57
00:05:03,548 --> 00:05:10,145
The announcement names production-scale inference and post-training as sources of lessons to share.
公告提到，将分享生产规模推理和后训练中获得的经验。

58
00:05:10,145 --> 00:05:13,411
It also names performance as a contribution area.
公告还将性能列为贡献领域。

59
00:05:13,411 --> 00:05:21,824
For our imagined team, the next question would be which project receives a change and what problem that change addresses.
对我们设想的团队来说，接下来要问的是：改动会落在哪个项目，解决什么问题。

60
00:05:21,824 --> 00:05:28,164
Ava: Before we look ahead, there's a second kind of contribution in this membership: governance.
Ava：展望未来之前，先说说这次会员身份涉及的另一类贡献：治理。

61
00:05:28,164 --> 00:05:36,038
A cloud provider can provide compute and code, while a Foundation member can also take part in setting direction.
云服务商可以提供算力和代码；作为基金会成员，还能参与制定方向。

62
00:05:36,038 --> 00:05:40,150
What formal role does Platinum membership give Nebius?
白金会员身份正式赋予 Nebius 什么角色？

63
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:44,757
Brian: Nebius gets 1 seat on the PyTorch Foundation Governing Board.
Brian：Nebius 获得 PyTorch 基金会理事会的一个席位。

64
00:05:44,757 --> 00:05:51,253
The Board sets policy through the Foundation's bylaws, mission, and vision statements.
理事会依据基金会章程、使命宣言和愿景声明制定政策。

65
00:05:51,253 --> 00:05:58,655
Those describe the broad scope of Foundation initiatives, its technical vision, and its direction.
这些文件界定基金会各项计划的总体范围、技术愿景和发展方向。

66
00:05:58,655 --> 00:06:01,044
That's a broad policy role.
这是一个范围广泛的政策制定角色。

67
00:06:01,044 --> 00:06:04,291
Ava: It's useful to keep that role in proportion.
Ava：也要恰当看待这个角色。

68
00:06:04,291 --> 00:06:09,457
A board seat tells us Nebius can participate in Foundation governance.
理事会席位说明 Nebius 可以参与基金会治理。

69
00:06:09,457 --> 00:06:15,804
By itself, it doesn't tell us what a future PyTorch or vLLM contribution will contain.
单凭这一点，无法知道它未来对 PyTorch 或 vLLM 的贡献具体是什么。

70
00:06:15,804 --> 00:06:21,098
There's also a Technical Advisory Council role in the announcement.
公告还提到了技术咨询委员会的角色。

71
00:06:21,098 --> 00:06:28,698
Brian: Ryan Hanrui Wang will join the board and represent Nebius on the Technical Advisory Council, or TAC.
Brian：Ryan Hanrui Wang 将加入理事会，并代表 Nebius 进入技术咨询委员会（TAC）。

72
00:06:28,698 --> 00:06:33,714
At Nebius, he leads inference, post-training, and agentic systems.
在 Nebius，他负责推理、后训练和智能体系统。

73
00:06:33,714 --> 00:06:41,968
Those responsibilities connect directly to the production experience the company says it plans to share.
这些职责与公司计划分享的生产实践经验直接相关。

74
00:06:41,968 --> 00:06:44,590
Ava: His technical background adds context.
Ava：他的技术经历也提供了更多背景。

75
00:06:44,590 --> 00:06:52,247
The announcement says he created the SpAtten sparse-attention framework and Hardware-Aware Transformers at MIT.
公告称，他在 MIT 创建了 SpAtten 稀疏注意力框架和 Hardware-Aware Transformers。

76
00:06:52,247 --> 00:07:01,566
That work sounds relevant to model systems, but it would be a leap to predict a specific project change from his earlier research.
这些研究与模型系统有关，但不能据此预测他会对某个项目做出什么具体改动。

77
00:07:01,566 --> 00:07:05,999
Brian: He also co-founded Eigen AI, which Nebius acquired in 2026.
Brian：他还联合创办了 Eigen AI，Nebius 于 2026 年收购了这家公司。

78
00:07:05,999 --> 00:07:14,340
The announcement says his open-source work has passed 1 million downloads and is part of the PyTorch Ecosystem.
公告称，他的开源成果下载量已超过 100 万次，且属于 PyTorch 生态系统的一部分。

79
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:22,580
Those details explain his connection to the community; the download count isn't a measure of performance.
这些信息说明了他与社区的联系；下载量并不代表性能。

80
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:28,494
Ava: So we have people, governance, and existing technical activity in one announcement.
Ava：这份公告同时涉及人员、治理和已有的技术工作。

81
00:07:28,494 --> 00:07:36,332
Ryan Hanrui Wang says Nebius wants deeper collaboration and an easier path from experimentation to production.
Ryan Hanrui Wang 说，Nebius 希望深化合作，让实验成果更容易进入生产环境。

82
00:07:36,332 --> 00:07:43,594
I read that as the company's aim, rather than a claim about any particular customer's transition.
我把这理解为公司的目标，而非对任何特定客户转型情况的断言。

83
00:07:43,594 --> 00:07:50,978
Brian: Mark Collier, the Foundation's Executive Director, frames the collaboration around scaling challenges.
Brian：基金会执行董事 Mark Collier 从规模化挑战的角度谈这项合作。

84
00:07:50,978 --> 00:07:58,290
He points to PyTorch and vLLM, high-throughput inference performance, and large-scale model training.
他提到了 PyTorch 和 vLLM、高吞吐量推理性能，以及大规模模型训练。

85
00:07:58,290 --> 00:08:06,096
That explains why the Foundation welcomes Nebius's participation across both training and serving work.
这说明基金会为何欢迎 Nebius 同时参与训练和模型服务工作。

86
00:08:06,096 --> 00:08:11,215
Ava: For our imagined team, the announcement is useful as a map of activity.
Ava：对我们设想的团队来说，这份公告有助于看清相关工作的分布。

87
00:08:11,215 --> 00:08:20,083
They can see where Nebius already provides cloud capacity or contributes to open source, and where it intends to work next.
他们能看到 Nebius 已在哪些方面提供云算力或参与开源，以及接下来计划做什么。

88
00:08:20,083 --> 00:08:24,254
It isn't enough on its own to choose a serving setup.
但仅凭这份公告，还不足以选择模型服务方案。

89
00:08:24,254 --> 00:08:29,309
Brian: Right. A technical choice would depend on the team's model and workload.
Brian：没错。技术选择取决于团队的模型和工作负载。

90
00:08:29,309 --> 00:08:37,734
The compute support for multi-node DeepSeek R1 work tells us Nebius has supported a particular kind of large-model work.
对多节点 DeepSeek R1 工作的算力支持，说明 Nebius 曾支持这类大模型工作。

91
00:08:37,734 --> 00:08:43,420
It doesn't transfer a performance result to a different model or deployment.
这并不意味着其他模型或部署也能取得相同的性能。

92
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:45,321
Ava: What would you look for next?
Ava：接下来你会关注什么？

93
00:08:45,321 --> 00:08:51,024
I'd start with a concrete contribution to PyTorch or vLLM and the problem it addresses.
我会先看对 PyTorch 或 vLLM 的具体贡献，以及它解决的问题。

94
00:08:51,024 --> 00:08:54,105
Then I'd ask whether it applies to my workload.
然后再看它是否适用于我的工作负载。

95
00:08:54,105 --> 00:09:00,354
That feels more actionable than trying to infer an improvement from the membership itself.
这比仅凭会员身份推测会有什么改进更有实际参考价值。

96
00:09:00,354 --> 00:09:06,608
Brian: I'd also watch how Nebius shares lessons from production-scale inference and post-training.
Brian：我也会关注 Nebius 如何分享生产规模推理和后训练的经验。

97
00:09:06,608 --> 00:09:13,343
The value for other engineers will depend on the details it can share and the changes that follow.
这些经验对其他工程师有多大价值，取决于它能分享的细节和后续的改动。

98
00:09:13,343 --> 00:09:15,680
That's a question for future work.
这还要看今后的工作。

99
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:20,360
Today's announcement establishes the plan and the formal roles.
今天的公告确定了计划和正式角色。

100
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,594
Ava: Here's my recap.
Ava：我来总结一下。

101
00:09:21,594 --> 00:09:32,775
Nebius already supports PyTorch training and fine-tuning on its cloud, provides compute for vLLM work, and contributes open-source optimizations.
Nebius 已在其云平台支持 PyTorch 训练和微调，为 vLLM 相关工作提供算力，并贡献开源优化成果。

102
00:09:32,775 --> 00:09:43,150
Platinum membership adds a Governing Board seat, with Ryan Hanrui Wang also representing Nebius on the Technical Advisory Council.
成为白金会员后，Nebius 将获得一个理事会席位，Ryan Hanrui Wang 也将代表 Nebius 加入技术咨询委员会。

103
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:53,674
Brian: And the next areas to watch are PyTorch and vLLM performance on the latest hardware platforms, plus lessons from production-scale inference and post-training.
Brian：接下来值得关注的是 PyTorch 和 vLLM 在最新硬件平台上的性能，以及生产规模推理和后训练的实践经验。

104
00:09:53,674 --> 00:09:57,870
Specific contributions will show what that means for engineers.
具体贡献将让工程师看清这意味着什么。

105
00:09:57,870 --> 00:10:01,284
Thanks for listening; we'll see you next time.
感谢收听，我们下次再见。
